start

Starts a local Cloud Datastore instance. <directory> must contain a valid
datastore project (created using the 'create' action) or be started with
--testing.

Usage: cloud_datastore_emulator start [options] [<directory]>

Options:
  --host=HOST
    The address to bind to on the local machine. Defaults to localhost.
  -p PORT, --port=PORT
    The port number to listen to on the local machine. Defaults to port 8080.
  --testing
    Start the local Cloud Datastore in 'testing' mode. Equivalent to passing
    --consistency=1.0 and --store_on_disk=false and
    --store_index_configuration_on_disk=false. Note that the testing option may 
    mask incorrect assumptions about the consistency of non-ancestor queries;
    non-ancestor queries are eventually consistent.
  --consistency=CONSISTENCY
    The fraction of job application attempts that will succeed, with 0.0
    resulting in no attempts succeeding, and 1.0 resulting in all attempts
    succeeding. Defaults to 0.9. Note that setting this to 1.0 may mask
    incorrect assumptions about the consistency of non-ancestor queries;
    non-ancestor queries are eventually consistent.
  --store_on_disk=true|false
    Indicates whether data should stored on disk. When set to false, data is
    stored in memory only. By default, data is stored on disk in
    <directory>/WEB-INF/appengine-generated/local_db.bin.
  --store_index_configuration_on_disk=true|false
    If this option is not specified or set to true, the presence of the '#
    AUTOGENERATED' line in <directory>/WEB-INF/index.yaml determines whether
    indexes will be automatically generated and the index configuration stored
    on disk. If that  file does not exist (such as in new projects created by
    this tool), indexes  will be automatically generated and the configuration
    stored on disk. Setting  this option to false suppresses the creation of the
    configuration file,  regardless of the settings in
    <directory>/WEB-INF/index.yaml.
  --storage_file=
    If this option is specified, use the provided storage file for storing local
    data. By default, data is stored on disk in <project
    directory>/WEB-INF/appengine-generated/local_db.bin.
  --index_file=
    If this option is specified, use the provided index file for the index.yaml.
    If this option is not specified, an index.yaml file will be created
    automatically in  <directory>/WEB-INF. Additional indexes will be added to
    the index.yaml file  if the index.yaml file contains the '# AUTOGENERATED'
    line.
  --allow_reserved_kinds
    Indicates whether the emulator whitelists some reserved kinds. This is for
    backward compatibility with ndb and blobstore tests.
  --require_indexes
    If this option is specified, for queries that require indexes not specified
    in the index file, the emulator will throw exception.
  --regenerate_indexes=true|false
    If this option is true, existing auto generated indexes will be fully
    regenerated based on query history, which will delete unused indexes.
  --auto_id_policy=SEQUENTIAL|SCATTERED
    Specifies how the emulator assigns auto id policy. Should be either
    SEQUENTIAL or SCATTERED
  --firestore_in_datastore_mode
    Runs the emulator in Cloud Firestore in Datastore Mode. --consistency flag
    is ignored.
  --enable_entity_groups=true|false
    If this option is set, the Datastore emulator with simulate entity groups
    for concurrency.

